Transport Energy Consumption — Gorbeialdea

Scripts and data supporting the MSc thesis "Analysis of the energy consumption 
of the transport in Gorbeialdea" (Erasmus Mundus Joint Master's in Smart Cities 
and Communities, SMACCs — UPV/EHU, University of Vaasa, University of Mons, 2026).

Contents

Scripts
- `build_link_table (1).py` constructs the road network link table from the 
  node table (prepared in QGIS from IGN IGR-RT road shapefiles) and the road 
  shapefile geometry, using geopandas and shapely.
- `od_matrix (1).py` — origin-destination matrix estimation using Tikhonov-regularised 
  Generalized Least Squares (TRLS), solved with scipy's bounded-variable least 
  squares (`lsq_linear`). The primary method retained in the thesis.
- `od_matrix (2).py` — origin-destination matrix estimation using the Khan and 
  Anderson (2014) constrained estimator. This method was tested and rejected in 
  the thesis due to fundamental divergence on the underdetermined system in this 
  study; it is included here for transparency and reproducibility of that finding, 
  not as a retained method.
- `od_matrix_ME2.py` — origin-destination matrix estimation using Entropy 
  Maximisation (ME2), the second method retained in the thesis.

Energy consumption scenario calculations (2024 / 2030 / 2050) were performed 
directly in Excel rather than Python; see the two scenario workbooks below.

Data
- `Link Table Final Updated.csv`, `Node Table Final Updated.csv` — road network 
  topology (links and nodes) ; see the thesis Section 3.1 for the full GIS workflow.
- `OD_matrix_results.xlsx` — estimated OD matrix, Tikhonov-regularised GLS (TRLS)
- `OD_matrix_results_ME2.xlsx` — estimated OD matrix, Entropy Maximisation (ME2)
- `link_flow_comparison.csv` — observed vs. estimated link flows, TRLS (supports Table 42 of the thesis)
- `link_flow_comparison_ME2.csv` — observed vs. estimated link flows, ME2 (supports Table 42 of the thesis)
- `regularisation_sensitivity.csv` — sensitivity sweep over the Tikhonov regularisation parameter (supports Table 41 of the thesis)
- `Gorbeialdea_Energy_Consumption_Scenarios_TRLS_Method.xlsx` — energy consumption 
  scenario results (2024 / 2030 / 2050), computed in Excel from the TRLS OD matrix
- `Gorbeialdea_Energy_Consumption_Scenarios_ME2_Method.xlsx` — energy consumption 
  scenario results (2024 / 2030 / 2050), computed in Excel from the ME² OD matrix

Requirements
Python scripts require: numpy, pandas, networkx, scipy, openpyxl, geopandas, shapely.

Data sources
Input AADT and vehicle registration data are drawn from the 2024 Álava provincial 
traffic map and the DGT municipal vehicle register. Raw source data is not 
redistributed here due to licensing; see the thesis Annex A and B for full source 
documentation.

Citation
If you use this code, please cite the thesis: 
Z. Zarqa, "Analysis of the energy consumption of the transport in Gorbeialdea," M.S. thesis, Erasmus Mundus Joint Master's in Smart Cities and Communities (SMACCs), Universidad del País Vasco / Euskal Herriko Unibertsitatea (UPV/EHU), Bilbao, Spain, 2026.

